-- Should type-check, but the checker aborts with
--   Fatal error: exception File "src/lang.ml", line 67, characters 4-10: Assertion failed
--
-- The tensor pair a ⊗ a splits the bunch with FV(a) on both sides. Since a is crisp, this is
-- allowed (crisp variables are shared, as in ♭(A ⨂ A) ≃ ♭(A × A)), but split asserts that the two
-- sides have disjoint free variables before crisp variables are discounted.
--
-- Compare test/fail/diag-tens.batt, the same term with a non-crisp a, which must fail; it
-- currently fails through this same assertion rather than through a split error.

crisp-diag ∷ (A ∷ U) (a ∷ A) → A ⨂ A
crisp-diag A a = a ⊗ a
